re infinitely many positive rational integer pairs ( l 1 , l 2 ) such that b l 1 1 /b l 2 2 is close to one. In fact, consider the set"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"P = { b l 1 1 /b l 2 2 : ( l 1 , l 2 ) ∈ Z 2 > 0 } ⊂ C .","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":124.37130808328527,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":221.77799999999985,"r":390.2228143999999,"t":139.5165783},"charspan":[0,56],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/79","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"footnote","orig":"3 In general, such a logarithmic map can be defined in each Galois embedding individually.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":92.2298898772334,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":126.672,"r":485.3223899600002,"t":115.39157829999999},"charspan":[0,90],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/80","text":"3 In general, such a logarithmic map can be defined in each Galois embedding individually."}],"version":"1.10.0"}